# Exmeralda Attached Livebook

## Setup

Livebook runs attached to the Exmeralda app. Just start exmeralda and livebook via:

```sh
./scripts/start
```

Then, open http://localhost:8080 and load `/data/attached_livebook.livemd`.

## Peek a code chunk

Raw SQL:

```elixir
sql = """
SELECT content, source, type
FROM chunks
WHERE type = 'code'
LIMIT 1

-- To peek a specific chunk by ID, use:
-- SELECT content, source, type FROM chunks WHERE id = '<chunk-id>';
"""

%Postgrex.Result{columns: cols, rows: [row]} = Exmeralda.Repo.query!(sql, [])

cols
|> Enum.zip(row)
|> Map.new()
```

Same thing via Ecto:

```elixir
import Ecto.Query
alias Exmeralda.Repo
alias Exmeralda.Topics.Chunk

from(c in Chunk, where: c.type == :code, select: %{content: c.content, source: c.source, type: c.type}, limit: 1)
|> Repo.one()
```

## Run generate_and_judge

Edit the values below, then run the cell.

```elixir
alias Exmeralda.Topics.Rag.Evaluation

query = "How do I decode a JSON string into a map with Jason?"
ingestion_id = "51ef61cb-65c3-42b2-95ed-0bf3fe1ccede"
env_a_id = "768417b2-1f1b-4a8c-a936-eb5502146d05"
env_b_id = "1667da4f-249a-4e23-ae13-85a4efa5d1f5"
judge_env_id = "a72fb346-f36d-4706-92f0-dc009980c435"

{:ok, result} =
  Evaluation.generate_and_judge(query, ingestion_id, env_a_id, env_b_id, judge_env_id)

IO.inspect(result, label: "\nresult", pretty: true, limit: :infinity, printable_limit: :infinity)
```
